---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy"
	description="Yeh Bro privacy overview — what we collect, analytics, email, and overseas processors."
>
	<article class="prose-wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			AU Privacy Act / APP-minded summary for a small static content site. Not a substitute for formal
			legal counsel.
		</p>

		<h2>What this site is</h2>
		<p>
			Yeh Bro publishes fitness and sports nutrition guides. The site is primarily static. We minimise
			personal data.
		</p>

		<h2>What we may collect</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Contact:</strong> if you email us, we receive whatever you send (name, address,
				message).
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Email list (planned):</strong> address and signup metadata via Beehiiv or similar —
				processed overseas.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Analytics (planned):</strong> privacy-friendly pageview analytics (e.g. Plausible or
				Cloudflare Web Analytics). We prefer tools that avoid invasive advertising cookies.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Server / host logs:</strong> standard request logs from Cloudflare or our host.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>What we don’t do (MVP)</h2>
		<p>
			No account system. No shop checkout on this domain. No Meta/TikTok pixels until paid ads are
			scheduled — and then only with appropriate consent.
		</p>

		<h2>Affiliate clicks</h2>
		<p>
			Clicks on <code>/go/</code> links send you to a third-party retailer. Their privacy policy
			applies on their site.
		</p>

		<h2>Overseas processors</h2>
		<p>
			Hosting, analytics, and email tools may store data outside Australia. We choose reputable
			providers and only collect what we need.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>Privacy questions: <a href="/contact">Contact</a>.</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
